<title>GREECE: Natl Mortgage Bank cuts mortgage rates.</title>
<headline>Natl Mortgage Bank cuts mortgage rates.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>State National Mortgage Bank said on Monday it will lower its mortgage rates by 0.25 to 0.50 basis points effective September 4.</p>
<p>It said its new rates (previous in brackets) will be:</p>
<p>    3-year mortgages			   15.50% (16.00)</p>
<p>    6-year mortgages			   16.00% (16.50)</p>
<p>    10, 15, 20-year fixed rate mortgages   16.75% (17.00)</p>
<p>10, 15, 20-year floating rate motgages 17.25% (17.50)</p>
<p>National Mortgage will also lower its deposit rates by 50 basis points.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite the rate cuts our deposit rates are still among the highest in the market,&quot; it said in a statement. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
